Description: SVG badge and glyph generator written in Guile Scheme
 GGG (Guile Glyph Generator) generates the SVG badges projects use to
 announce the technologies they build with, the versions they support and
 the projects they appreciate.
 .
 Badges are described in ordinary Scheme files, can have one, two or three
 sections, and are rendered from S-expressions, so a badge is a value in
 your build rather than a screenshot.  Converting the badges to PNG is
 optional and is done with ImageMagick, falling back to Inkscape.
